        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="v41" value="&lt;b&gt;IDENTITIES (Task 1)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ID-1&lt;/b&gt; Human user (customer / admin): Customer: read:ai-data&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ID-2&lt;/b&gt; AI agent (Orchestrator Agent A + Action Agent B): Acts on behalf of the signed-in user, so it should never hold more than the user&amp;#x27;s own scope (read:ai-data)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ID-3&lt;/b&gt; OAuth M2M client (Action Agent B): read:ai-data on the Internal REST APIs&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ID-4&lt;/b&gt; LLM API key: Full inference on the provider account: every model, spend up to the account limit&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ID-5&lt;/b&gt; RAG pipeline service identity: Query: read-only on the vector store, filtered by tenant&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ID-6&lt;/b&gt; MCP server identity: Per-tool scopes on an allow-list (for example tickets:read, refunds:create up to a limit)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;User layer TB1 -&gt; Agent layer TB4 via F04, F06. Agent layer TB4 -&gt; Internal API layer TB5 via F15, F16 -&gt; F17.&lt;br&gt;Red dashed box = trust boundary. Every flow has 6 STRIDE entries (STRIDE-Matrix.xlsx)." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;spacing=6;strokeColor=#999999;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="720" width="860" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="v42" value="&lt;b&gt;SecureNova AI Customer Service Platform - Identity data-flow diagram&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;fontSize=18;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="-30" width="900" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
